  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;denote the number of solutions of the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> is a complex number. Then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>&#8734;</mo></munderover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mfrac></math> is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Put&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then we know that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;hence, we have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>We also, know that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;hence, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>On comparing the real and imaginary parts, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>And&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Put <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> in equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>27</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Now, put&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;in the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> No of solutions<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>&#8734;</mo></munderover><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>&#8734;</mo></munderover><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>64</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo></math></p><p>The above progression is a geometric progression, with first term&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and common ratio&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and the sum of infinite terms of the geometric progression is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Thus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>&#8734;</mo></munderover><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
  }
}